  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Somalia is facing a severe drought-driven humanitarian crisis in 2026, characterized by worsening water scarcity, food insecurity, malnutrition, displacement, and rapidly deteriorating livelihood conditions. According to the Federal Government of Somalia and the United Nations 6.5 million people are experiencing Crisis (IPC 3) or worse levels of food insecurity, including around 2 million in Emergency (IPC 4). An estimated 1.84 million children under five are expected to suffer from acute malnut</narrative>
